## Alert Processing Pipeline

Every security event follows this path:

```
1. DETECTION
   Falco (runtime syscalls)  â”€â”€â†’  Falco Forwarder  â”€â”€â†’  POST /api/alerts/internal
   Suricata (network sigs)   â”€â”€â†’  Suricata Forwarder â”€â†’  POST /api/alerts/internal
   Dashboard buttons / CLI   â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â†’  POST /api/alerts/internal

2. INTAKE (main.py)
   â”œâ”€ Rate limiter: per-rule (10/min), per-source (100/min), global (500/min)
   â”‚  â””â”€ Exceeds â†’ HTTP 429, stored in throttled_alerts table
   â”œâ”€ Request queue: max 100 concurrent
   â”‚  â””â”€ Full â†’ HTTP 503
   â”œâ”€ Source detection: classify alert as "falco" or "suricata"
   â””â”€ Dedup cache: MD5(rule + proc.cmdline + container.name), 60s TTL
      â””â”€ Cache hit â†’ return cached analysis, skip LLM call

3. LLM ANALYSIS (llm_manager.py)
   â”œâ”€ Circuit breaker check (per-engine, threshold=5 failures, 30s recovery)
   â”œâ”€ Cooldown check (15min after quota/auth errors)
   â”œâ”€ Try engines in priority order: xai â†’ openai â†’ kimi â†’ local
   â”‚  â””â”€ Each: build prompt â†’ API call â†’ parse JSON â†’ validate
   â””â”€ Output: {severity, threat_type, summary, recommendations, automated_actions}

4. AUTOMATED RESPONSE (k8s_automation.py + governance.py)
   â”œâ”€ severity â‰¥ 8 â†’ isolate_pod (NetworkPolicy, unless protected service)
   â”œâ”€ severity â‰¥ 6 â†’ scale_up (replicas to 5)
   â””â”€ Governance: autopilot (all auto) / assisted (sev<8 auto) / manual (all approval)

5. PERSISTENCE (database.py)
   â”œâ”€ PostgreSQL: alerts, analysis_results, automation_actions, audit_logs
   â”œâ”€ Memory fallback if PostgreSQL unavailable
   â””â”€ Prometheus counters restored from DB on restart
```

### Pipeline-to-Metrics Mapping (Dashboard)

The Overview "Pipeline Overview" row maps each stage to concrete metrics:

| Stage | Metric / Source | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Falco alerts | `smartcity_ids_alerts_raw_total{source="falco"}` | Raw ingress rate before dedup/throttling |
| Suricata alerts | `smartcity_ids_alerts_raw_total{source="suricata"}` | Raw network alert ingress |
| IDS ingest + dedup | `smartcity_ids_alerts_after_dedup_total`, `smartcity_ids_dedup_hit_rate_percent` | Shows analysis workload after dedup |
| LLM / local analysis | `smartcity_ids_llm_requests_total{engine,result}`, `smartcity_ids_llm_latency_seconds` | p95 latency and per-engine throughput |
| Governance + K8s actions | `smartcity_ids_human_review_required_total`, `smartcity_ids_actions_executed_total` | Analyst touch vs automated response |

Additional LLM observability exported by IDS API:

- `smartcity_ids_llm_tokens_total{engine,kind="prompt|completion"}` (estimated tokens)
- `smartcity_ids_llm_cost_usd_total{engine}` (estimated total cost)
- `/api/llm-stats/export` provides per-engine aggregate latency, token, and cost summaries used by UI tables.

