## 7. Security Response Performance

### 7.1 Automated Response Matrix

| Severity | Action | Description | Latency |
|----------|--------|-------------|---------|
| â‰¥ 8 (Critical) | Pod Isolation | Network policy applied to isolate compromised pod | <5s |
| â‰¥ 6 (High) | Service Scale-Up | Increase replicas of target service | <10s |
| â‰¥ 4 (Medium) | Alert + Log | Log warning, notify analyst | <2s |
| < 4 (Low) | Log Only | Record for audit trail | <1s |

### 7.2 Before vs. After Comparison

| Metric | Before (Traditional IDS) | After (LLM-Driven IDS) | Improvement |
|--------|-------------------------|------------------------|-------------|
| Daily alert volume (analyst) | 10,000+ | 500â€“1,000 | 10â€“20Ã— reduction |
| Mean Time to Respond | 5â€“15 minutes | 30â€“60 seconds | 10â€“30Ã— faster |
| False positive rate | 40â€“60% | 10â€“15% | 3â€“4Ã— reduction |
| Analyst context per alert | Rule name only | Full narrative + reasoning | Qualitative leap |
| Overnight coverage | None | Full automation | 24/7 coverage |
| Cost per alert processed | ~$0.50 (analyst time) | ~$0.01 (LLM API) | 50Ã— cheaper |

