### Figure 3 â€” Circuit Breaker State Machine

> **PLACE IN:** Section 4.3.2 "Circuit Breaker State Machine" (report line ~406)
> **PLACE AFTER:** The text block that describes the three states (`CLOSED â†’ OPEN â†’ HALF_OPEN â†’ CLOSED`). Place the figure right below that description.
> **CAPTION:** "Figure 3: Circuit breaker state machine for LLM provider health management. Each provider maintains an independent circuit breaker with a 5-failure threshold and 30-second cooldown period."

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Closed : System startup

    Closed --> Open : failure_count â‰¥ 5
    Closed --> Closed : success â†’ reset counter to 0

    Open --> HalfOpen : 30-second cooldown expires

    HalfOpen --> Closed : Test request succeeds â†’ reset
    HalfOpen --> Open : Test request fails â†’ restart timer

    state Closed {
        [*] --> NormalOps
        NormalOps : âœ… All requests forwarded to provider
        NormalOps : ðŸ“Š Track consecutive failures (0â€“4)
        NormalOps : ðŸ”„ Each success resets counter to 0
    }

    state Open {
        [*] --> Blocked
        Blocked : ðŸš« ALL requests immediately fail-fast
        Blocked : â±ï¸ 30-second cooldown timer running
        Blocked : â†—ï¸ Requests routed to next provider
        Blocked : ðŸ“ˆ PROM_CIRCUIT_BREAKER_TRIPS incremented
    }

    state HalfOpen {
        [*] --> Probing
        Probing : ðŸ§ª Single test request allowed through
        Probing : âœ… Success â†’ transition to Closed
        Probing : âŒ Failure â†’ transition back to Open
    }
```

